#!RuleTest
#test CDISC-SEND-0106.1 expect=noViolation domain=DM
#note "GROUPED-PATH ZERO-ROW PIN (PLAN-leaf-scope-domain-inference.md Q12 ruling (c), 2026-08-22). A Group-sensitivity rule returns into RuleRunner.executeGrouped BEFORE the rowBased gate, and executeGrouped builds NO synthetic 1-row zero-column table: a 0-row DM has no group to evaluate, so the rule is EXECUTED with zero findings even though STRAIN is blank-by-absence everywhere (DM declares the column with no rows; TS and TX carry no STRAIN parameter). This is the cell the Fix #330 bare-emptiness retirement could NOT reach: `empty(STRAIN)` would fold TRUE on the synthetic table, but no Group rule ever sees that table. Written from the OBSERVED run, not the expectation; re-adjudicate under PLAN-zero-row-routing-rekey.md if the grouped path's zero-row behaviour is ever re-keyed."
#library standard=sendig version=3-1-1
dataset DM label="Demographics" class="SPECIAL PURPOSE"
col STUDYID type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col DOMAIN  type=Char label="Domain Abbreviation"
col USUBJID type=Char label="Unique Subject Identifier"
col SETCD   type=Char label="Set Code"
col SPECIES type=Char label="Species"
col STRAIN  type=Char label="Strain/Substrain"
col SEX     type=Char label="Sex"
---
---

dataset TS label="Trial Summary" class="TRIAL DESIGN"
col STUDYID  type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col DOMAIN   type=Char label="Domain Abbreviation"
col TSSEQ    type=Num  label="Sequence Number"
col TSPARMCD type=Char label="Trial Summary Parameter Short Name"
col TSPARM   type=Char label="Trial Summary Parameter"
col TSVAL    type=Char label="Parameter Value"
---
S1 | TS | 1 | TITLE  | Trial Title      | Study X
---

dataset TX label="Trial Sets" class="TRIAL DESIGN"
col STUDYID  type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col DOMAIN   type=Char label="Domain Abbreviation"
col SETCD    type=Char label="Set Code"
col TXSEQ    type=Num  label="Sequence Number"
col TXPARMCD type=Char label="Trial Set Parameter Short Name"
col TXPARM   type=Char label="Trial Set Parameter"
col TXVAL    type=Char label="Parameter Value"
---
S1 | TX | SET01 | 1 | GRPLBL | Group Label | Control
---
